{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The electrical connector kit fits my battery-holder and relay projects because it could help me make power connections, although the assortment is larger than I need.",
    "The shielded cable feels like a plausible next purchase for low-current signal wiring alongside my breadboards and circuit-board supplies, provided its specifications fit the project."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The hose fitting, coolant-hose pliers, and pipe tap require specific plumbing or machining tasks that my electronics purchases do not suggest.",
    "The lubricants do not address a maintenance need I have expressed; buying casters alone does not mean I need oil. Painter's tape and polishing supplies likewise lack a clear role in my current projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical project supplies seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop item.",
    "My caster purchase seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest general mechanical supplies, even though I choose those only when a particular task calls for them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my purchases work together around small electronics: breadboards, a battery holder, circuit boards, jumper wires, and a relay. Supplies that connect or support those parts feel more relevant.",
    "I need a clear use and compatible specifications before choosing a specialized part or a large assortment; general usefulness is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly recognized my electronics projects but broadened that interest too far into unrelated workshop and maintenance needs."
}"}
